[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Extended tree-sitter support for sdoc

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-SDOC-TREE-SITTER-SUPPORT
TITLE: Extended tree-sitter support for sdoc
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The umbrella for extended tree-sitter/sdoc support, carrying three build items
and a set of unsettled use cases the operator listed but did not settle. The
build items: a tree-sitter grammar for the sdoc format itself, derived from
the sdoc grammar (WORK-SDOC-TREE-SITTER-GRAMMAR); letting a field embed
another language, named by a companion field
(WORK-SDOC-EMBEDDED-LANGUAGE-FIELDS); and extending the sdoc tree-sitter
grammar to switch its inner grammar on that language field
(WORK-SDOC-GRAMMAR-LANGUAGE-SWITCH). The unsettled use cases this could serve
-- assembling output documents from chunks, presentation nodes with syntax
highlighting, work items that are literal bash scripts, and matching,
highlighting, and extracting inner sdocs found in code comments -- are filed
as their own WORK-UC-* children rather than folded into the build items, since
the operator raised them as open uses to weigh, not requirements.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-02, verbatim: "two more sdocs from my drive home. - sdoc
grammars to custom tree-sitter grammar - allow fields to contain other
languages embedded, maybe with another field for the language. - extend sdoc
treesitter grammar to support switching lang grammar based on above. can
maybe parent under one node for extended tree-sitter/sdoc support. unsettled
use cases: - assembling output docs from chunks (e.g., md). - presentation
nodes with like syntax highlighting - work items that are literal bash
scripts - match inner sdocs in code comments - syntax highlighting -
extraction"
<<<
